Since $AC=BC$, the base angles are equal.
$$\begin{align*}
\angle CAB&=\frac{180^{\circ}-80^{\circ}}{2}\\
&=50^{\circ}
\end{align*}$$
Hence $\angle ABC=50^{\circ}$. The angle from north at $A$ to $AB$ is also $50^{\circ}$ (alternate angles on parallel north lines). The bearing is $050^{\circ}$.

The north lines are parallel, so the angle clockwise from north at $A$ to $AC$ and the $80^{\circ}$ angle at $C$ are cointerior angles.
$$\begin{align*}
\text{Bearing of }C\text{ from }A&=180^{\circ}-80^{\circ}\\
&=100^{\circ}
\end{align*}$$

Since $AC=BC$, $\angle ABC=(180^{\circ}-80^{\circ})\div2=50^{\circ}$. The angle anticlockwise from north at $B$ to $BA$ is $180^{\circ}-50^{\circ}=130^{\circ}$ (angles on a straight line).
$$\begin{align*}
\text{Bearing of }A\text{ from }B&=360^{\circ}-130^{\circ}\\
&=230^{\circ}
\end{align*}$$

